  "id": "orchestration/a-two-word-mark-opening-written-as-one-identifier-is-code-not-a-copy",
  "title": "A two-word mark opening written as one token, no space or invisible character between its words (conversation_summary, ConversationSummary, conversation.summary, conversation-summary), is code and reaches the model as written behind any bracket, in a call, a subscript, a JSON key, a type, a path, a code block or a TOML table; the same opening with a space or an invisible character between its words is a copy behind any bracket, at a line's start or glued to a word, and a longer opening counts however its words are joined",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4"
  ],
  "notes": "HITL 2edb51ef (option A): since HITL 0e813328 a mark's opening counts behind any opening bracket, which rewrote code and JSON naming conversation_summary in both implementations (Python channels/_mark_copies.py, roomkit-rs marks.rs). The narrowing proposed to the maintainer: a two-word opening written as one token is an identifier. One room per message, so each generation reads one message. A braille blank (U+2800) or an invisible character Python counts as one (U+17B4, U+034F) between the two words is a word break: the copy counts, in a short mark as in a long one (review of the lot, HITL f77ed389).",
